 "_comment": [
  "WHAT FRACTION OF AZTEC TESTNET HISTORY IS ACTUALLY TRACEABLE, measured rather than",
  "estimated. The standing claim this replaces was CHAIN-CAPTURE.md §1: \"a batch job over",
  "history is not a slow version of the right design; it is a thing that cannot work.\"",
  "",
  "FIVE WHOLE WINDOWS, NOT A SAMPLE OF TRANSACTIONS. Every transaction the chain published",
  "in each 200-block window was attempted. Sampling within a window would have let the",
  "selection carry the result; sampling WINDOWS is a stated limitation and is why the",
  "per-window rows are published beside the total rather than only the total.",
  "",
  "THREE DENOMINATORS AND THEY ARE ALL DIFFERENT. `transactions` is everything the chain",
  "published. `firstInBlock` removes the ones no node method can serve intermediate state",
  "for. `withPublicHalf` removes the private-only ones, which have no public execution to",
  "trace at all. A single \"yield\" figure quoted without saying which of the three it is",
  "over is the number this file exists to stop being quoted."
